Attributions
============

1. EasyOCR (JaidedAI)
---------------------
The recognition model's lineage traces to the EasyOCR "gen2" recognition
architecture. EasyOCR is NOT a runtime dependency of the `olchiki-ocr` core
(the core runs on ONNX Runtime), but the model heritage and gen2 architecture
influence are attributed here.

    EasyOCR
    Copyright (c) Jaided AI (https://github.com/JaidedAI/EasyOCR)
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0


2. deep-text-recognition-benchmark (DTRB / clovaai)
---------------------------------------------------
The recognition model uses the DTRB `None-VGG-BiLSTM-CTC` architecture and was
trained/fine-tuned with the clovaai deep-text-recognition-benchmark training
scripts. DTRB is not pip-installable; the `[train]` tier obtains it via a
pinned external git clone at commit
`e2117f2fb882b3c6085030500a260c113be27a63`.

    deep-text-recognition-benchmark
    Copyright (c) 2019-present NAVER Corp. (https://github.com/clovaai/deep-text-recognition-benchmark)
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0


3. Noto Sans Ol Chiki fonts
---------------------------
The model's weights were produced from synthetic training images rendered with
the Noto Sans Ol Chiki font family (Regular, Bold, Medium, SemiBold), part of
the Google Noto Fonts project.

    Noto Sans Ol Chiki
    Part of the Google Noto Fonts project.
